        "thought_text": "Use nested loops where the outer loop processes each student and the inner loop checks all M checkpoints, updating the best checkpoint index whenever a strictly smaller distance is found or when distances are equal but the current checkpoint index is smaller (though the problem guarantees we check in order 1 to M, so strict inequality suffices if we initialize correctly).",
